# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same keys in Vercel
# (Project → Settings → Environment Variables).
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is the dividing line and it is not cosmetic. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ value
# is INLINED INTO THE CLIENT BUNDLE at build time — public by design, and changing one needs
# a REDEPLOY, not just a saved env var. Everything else is server-side only: mark it
# "Sensitive" in Vercel and never add the prefix to it. Where a key is public by design
# (Google Maps, the Stripe publishable key, the Turnstile site key), restrict it at the
# provider rather than trying to hide it.

# Google Maps — address autocomplete on the installation booking wizard.
# Restrict the key by HTTP referrer to the FineVu domains in Google Cloud.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# Resend — sends contact / retailer / services form submissions server-side to
# support@finevuaustralia.com.au (via app/api/contact). SECRET — never prefix with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, and mark it "Sensitive" in Vercel. Get the key at https://resend.com
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Overrides for the contact route. CONTACT_TO_EMAIL defaults to
# support@finevuaustralia.com.au; CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL defaults to onboarding@resend.dev.
#
# finevuaustralia.com.au IS verified in Resend as of 2026-08-13, so the old "Resend only
# permits onboarding@resend.dev" restriction no longer applies. SET CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL to
# the verified domain — until you do, the fallback is what actually sends, and it is meant
# to be a fail-safe rather than the production sender. It is read by both senders
# (app/api/contact and the booking confirmation).
#
# ⚠️ CONTACT_TO_EMAIL is where EVERY contact enquiry, product registration, warranty claim
# and retailer application lands. There is no database, so for those four forms that inbox
# IS the record. As of 2026-08-13 nobody has access to it, so no submission has ever been
# confirmed to arrive and the launch check "submit the form once and confirm it lands"
# cannot be run. Sort mailbox access before treating the forms as working (FB-08).
# CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=support@finevuaustralia.com.au
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=FineVu Australia <no-reply@finevuaustralia.com.au>

# ── Cloudflare Turnstile — CAPTCHA on the four email forms (FB-07) ───────────────────
# The honeypot alone only catches naive bots: a scripted POST that omits the botcheck
# field walks straight past it. Turnstile is the durable check. From Cloudflare →
# Turnstile → Add site; one widget covers all four forms.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY  drawn by components/Turnstile.tsx. Public by design.
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY            verified server-side in app/api/contact/route.ts.
#                                   SECRET — mark it Sensitive in Vercel.
#
# ⚠️ IT FAILS OPEN WHEN UNSET, AND SILENTLY (FA-34). With no secret key, verification is
# SKIPPED and every form still submits successfully — no error, no log line, no visible
# difference. That is deliberate so local dev works without a Cloudflare account, but it
# means a production deploy missing these has NO CAPTCHA while looking completely healthy.
# SET BOTH TOGETHER, and confirm at launch that a POST with no turnstileToken is actually
# rejected with a 403. Do not treat "the forms still work" as evidence it is on.
#
# (A network error reaching Cloudflare fails CLOSED — that path is safe. It is only the
# absent-key path that waves submissions through.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Durable rate limit for /api/contact (FB-07). The route always enforces a best-effort
# in-memory limit; pointing it at a shared Upstash Redis store makes that ceiling global
# across serverless instances (in-memory is per-instance and resets on cold start).
# Provision via Vercel → Marketplace → Upstash (free tier is ample). Unset ⇒ in-memory
# fallback only. Vercel KV's KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN are accepted too.
# Both are server-only secrets — never prefix NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# …or the Vercel KV equivalents, read as a fallback in route.ts:80-81. Set ONE pair.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# ── Booking + payments — /installation step 5 (FB-01) ────────────────────────────────
# Three subsystems, and THEY MUST BE SET TOGETHER. The wizard takes a hold on a real GHL
# calendar slot, charges $250 through Stripe, and confirms the booking from the Stripe
# webhook. Miss any of them and the flow breaks in a way the customer only discovers at
# step 5, after filling in the whole wizard.
#
# Stripe — from Dashboard → Developers → API keys. Use TEST keys (sk_test_ / pk_test_)
# everywhere except production; scripts/e2e-booking.mjs refuses to run against a live key.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  mounts embedded Checkout. Public by design.
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY                   server-side. SECRET — Sensitive in Vercel.
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET               signing secret for app/api/stripe/webhook.
# The webhook secret is per-endpoint, so the value differs between local and production:
# locally it comes from `stripe listen` (npm run dev:booking prints it and checks it
# matches); in production it comes from Dashboard → Developers → Webhooks → your endpoint
# at https://<domain>/api/stripe/webhook. A mismatch 400s every delivery, so payments
# succeed and NOTHING IS EVER CONFIRMED — the slot stays held and no email goes out.
# Subscribe the endpoint to: checkout.session.completed, checkout.session.expired,
# charge.refunded.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# GoHighLevel — the installation calendar. Availability, the hold, and the confirmed
# booking all live here; the site has no database, so this IS the booking record.
#   GHL_API_KEY      private integration token. SECRET — Sensitive in Vercel.
#   GHL_LOCATION_ID  the sub-account the calendar belongs to.
#   GHL_CALENDAR_ID  the Installation Booking calendar itself.
# All three are server-side — the browser must never hold the token, which is why
# /api/booking/slots exists at all. NEVER prefix any of them with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# ⚠️ AVAILABILITY FAILS OPEN WHEN THESE ARE UNSET (FA-35). /api/booking/slots answers
# "not_configured" and the wizard falls back to showing every future weekday as bookable
# with nine invented time slots — indistinguishable from real availability. Intended for
# local dev only; a production deploy missing these advertises a month of dates that do
# not exist.
GHL_API_KEY=
GHL_LOCATION_ID=
GHL_CALENDAR_ID=

# Optional — where scripts/e2e-booking.mjs points. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Test-inbox redirect for the booking confirmation email. When set, EVERY booking
# confirmation goes to this address instead of the customer, with the real recipient in
# the subject and a banner in the body. Lets you read the real rendered email before the
# sending domain is verified.
# MUST BE UNSET IN PRODUCTION — leaving it set silently diverts every customer's booking
# confirmation and tax invoice to one inbox.
# The old caveat here — that Resend's sandbox only delivered to the account owner — no
# longer applies now the domain is verified (2026-08-13), so this can point anywhere. That
# makes leaving it set MORE dangerous: it will now silently deliver every customer's
# confirmation and tax invoice to one inbox instead of erroring out.
# BOOKING_EMAIL_REDIRECT_TO=you@example.com

# Legal entity details for the installation tax invoice (lib/data/business.ts).
# BUSINESS_ABN is REQUIRED before the first live payment — the code falls back to the
# placeholder "00 000 000 000", and an invoice bearing that is not a valid tax invoice.
# A sale over $82.50 inc GST must show the seller's ABN, and installation is $250.
# Set the same ABN on the Stripe account so its invoice matches ours.
# BUSINESS_ABN=12 345 678 901
# Set to "false" ONLY if the entity is not registered for GST — the invoice then omits
# the GST line entirely. Registration is separate from holding an ABN.
# BUSINESS_GST_REGISTERED=true

# Search-engine visibility. Unset or anything other than "true" = the site is NOT
# indexed (noindex via meta robots + X-Robots-Tag header). Fail-safe by design.
# Set to "true" ONLY when the site is meant to rank publicly in Google.
SITE_INDEXABLE=false

# Which site.config variant this build ships. Unset (or anything other than "staging")
# = the production config in config/site.config.ts, with the Coming Soon gate active.
# Set to "staging" in the staging Vercel project to layer config/site.config.staging.ts
# on top (nothing gated). Fail-safe by design: a typo yields the gated production config.
# Must be NEXT_PUBLIC_ — ComingSoonGate and Navigation are client components.
# Staging should keep SITE_INDEXABLE unset, so it never competes with production in search.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ENV=staging

# ── Firmware / manual downloads (Cloudflare R2) ──────────────────────────────────────
# The bucket is PRIVATE — no public URL, no custom domain. app/api/firmware/[id] signs a
# 5-minute download URL per request and redirects to it, so the files are served from
# finevuaustralia.com.au/api/firmware/... and the bucket is never publicly readable.
# Object keys live in `modelReleases` (lib/data/firmware.ts); nothing here names a file.
#
# From Cloudflare → R2 → Manage API Tokens → Create token. Scope it "Object Read only"
# and to the ONE firmware bucket — not account-wide, and never read/write.
# The token screen shows FOUR values; the big "Token value" is for Cloudflare's REST API
# and is NOT used here. Take these instead:
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID        the 32-char hex inside the S3 endpoint it shows you,
#                        https://<THIS>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com — not secret, it is in
#                        every dashboard URL.
#   R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID     shown as "Access Key ID" (32 chars).
#   R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY shown as "Secret Access Key" (64 chars). SHOWN ONCE — if you lose
#                        it you must roll a new token. Mark it Sensitive in Vercel.
#   R2_BUCKET            the bucket NAME, e.g. finevu-firmware. Not a URL, no slashes.
# All four are server-side. NEVER prefix any of them with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=

# The on/off switch for the download UI. "true" renders the pickers on /gx4k and /gx35 and
# the download rows on /support; anything else hides every tab, which makes the whole
# FirmwareDownloads section render nothing.
#
# SET IT ONLY WHERE THE FOUR R2 VARS ABOVE ARE ALSO SET — this draws the buttons, they make
# them work. Unset is the fail-safe state and the kill switch: clear it in Vercel to pull
# the downloads without touching code.
#
# It must be NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the product pages and /support are client components and
# cannot read server env. That means it is inlined at build time: changing it needs a
# REDEPLOY, not just a saved env var.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIRMWARE_DOWNLOADS=true
